      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While natural remedies like oregano oil capsules and cranberry extract can sometimes help with mild symptoms of urinary tract infections (UTIs) due to their anti-inflammatory and antibacterial properties, they might not be sufficient if you have a severe infection. UTIs often require antibiotics for proper treatment to avoid complications. You should consider seeing a healthcare professional to assess your symptoms accurately. If you wish to wait before taking antibiotics, your doctor might suggest supportive care and lifestyle changes while monitoring your condition for any worsening. Your health is very important, and professional guidance is the best course of action.",
